.TH CYAML_DECLARE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cyaml_declare \- declare an uninitialized cyaml variable
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

cyaml_declare(var_name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declare a cyaml handle variable named var_name, without initializing
it.  The macro exists so that the naming convention matches the other
c_collections modules, each of which has its own _declare macro.

This macro expands to "cyaml var_name".
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
var_name  Name of the variable to declare.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cyaml_declare(root);
root = cyaml_parse("key: value\en", NULL);
/* ... use root ... */
cyaml_destroy(root);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_declare_scoped (3),
.BR cyaml_destroy (3)
